---
// Figure 5: measured reads through the death of one primary, in three configurations.
import SimFigure from '../shared/SimFigure.astro';
import Choice from '../shared/Choice.astro';
import Readout from '../shared/Readout.astro';
import './cluster.css';
interface Props { number: number }
const { number } = Astro.props;
---
<SimFigure number={number} id="cluster-failover" title="What clients saw when one primary died" controls="none"
  caption="Measured on my laptop with Redis 8.10.3 and the default cluster-node-timeout of 15 seconds: three primaries, killed with kill -9 at time 0; six redis-py cluster clients, two per shard, each reading its own shard's keys at 300 a second; successful reads counted in half-second buckets, shown as reads a second. A client's reads often fall either side of a bucket boundary, so neighbouring buckets wobble in pairs (450 and 750, say) that still average 600. One run of each; detection took 17 to 20 seconds across four runs. Left out: writes lost in a failover, and how a different timeout or a real network changes the times.">
  <Fragment slot="params">
    <Choice name="scenario" label="The primary that died" value="replica"
      options={[{ value: 'replica', label: 'had a replica' }, { value: 'nocover', label: 'had no replica' }, { value: 'partial', label: 'had no replica; full coverage off' }]} />
  </Fragment>
  <Fragment slot="stats">
    <Readout name="failed" label="Its keys unavailable" kind="error" />
    <Readout name="others" label="Other shards' keys unavailable" kind="hit" />
  </Fragment>
  <div data-chart></div>
  <Fragment slot="text">
    <p>With a replica: reads of the dead primary's keys failed for 21 seconds. The other nodes agreed it had failed (the FAIL flag) 20.0 seconds after the kill, its replica won the election 1.1 seconds later, and reads resumed. Reads of the two healthy shards also stopped for about one second, between the failure being agreed and the replica taking over, because each node refuses all requests while any slot is unassigned or owned by a node marked as failed.</p>
    <p>Without a replica, and with the default cluster-require-full-coverage yes: once the failure was agreed, 19.9 seconds after the kill, the whole cluster stopped serving. Reads of the healthy shards' keys failed with CLUSTERDOWN from then until the end of the run, and would have gone on failing until someone repaired the cluster.</p>
    <p>Without a replica, with cluster-require-full-coverage no: the dead shard's keys stayed unavailable, but the other two shards served every read throughout.</p>
  </Fragment>
</SimFigure>
<script>
  import { bindParams, setReadouts } from '../shared/player.mjs';
  import { lineChart } from '../shared/chart.mjs';
  import { seriesFor, EVENTS } from './failover-data.mjs';

  document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-figure-id="cluster-failover"]').forEach(root => {
    const chart = lineChart(root.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-chart]')!, {
      label: 'Successful reads a second, before and after one primary was killed at time 0',
      height: 240,
      x: { label: 'Seconds after the kill', domain: [-6, 30], tickStep: 6 },
      y: { label: 'Reads a second per shard', domain: [0, 900], ticks: [0, 300, 600, 900] },
      series: [
        { id: 'failed', label: 'Keys on the shard whose primary died', kind: 'error' },
        { id: 'others', label: 'Keys on the other two shards (average)', kind: 'hit' },
      ],
    });
    const seconds = (v: number, open: boolean, from: string) => open ? `${from} until repaired` : v === 0 ? 'never' : `${v} s`;
    bindParams(root, (params: any) => {
      const scenario = params.scenario as keyof typeof EVENTS;
      const s = seriesFor(scenario);
      const event: any = EVENTS[scenario];
      chart.set('failed', s.failed);
      chart.set('others', s.others);
      chart.band('detect', 0, event.detected, 'detecting', 'neutral');
      chart.mark('fail', event.detected, 'FAIL', 'error');
      if (event.promoted) chart.mark('promoted', event.promoted, 'promoted', 'hit');
      else chart.mark('promoted', null);
      chart.render();
      setReadouts(root, {
        failed: seconds(s.failedDown, !event.promoted, 'from the kill'),
        others: seconds(s.othersDown, scenario === 'nocover', `from ${Math.round(event.detected)} s`),
      });
    });
  });
</script>
